## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py
  - Shows usage of ArxivToolkit with ChatAgent
  - Demonstrates searching and downloading papers like "attention is all you need"
  - Uses ModelFactory with default model and ModelPlatformType.DEFAULT
  - Shows how to get tools from ArxivToolkit and pass to ChatAgent

- examples/rag/single_agent_with_hybrid_rag.py
  - Shows example of single agent using HybridRetriever for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)
  - Demonstrates querying with vector retrieval and passing retrieved context to ChatAgent

- examples/memories/agent_memory_vector_db_example.py
  - Example usage of agent memory with vector database memory
  - Relevant for vector retrieval integration with agents

- examples/memories/vector_db_memory_example.py
  - Example usage of vector database memory block
  - Shows how to use vector embeddings and vector storage for memory

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py
  - Class: ArxivToolkit
  - Implements arXiv paper search, download, and text extraction
  - Provides tools: search_papers, download_papers

- camel/memories/blocks/vectordb_block.py
  - Class: VectorDBBlock
  - Implements vector database memory block with embedding and vector storage
  - Supports retrieve and write_records methods for vector retrieval

- camel/agents/chat_agent.py
  - Class: ChatAgent
  - Core agent class supporting tools, memory, model management, and interaction

## Enums (for exact values)
- camel/types/enums.py
  - ModelPlatformType: DEFAULT, OPENAI, TOGETHER, etc.
  - ModelType: DEFAULT, GPT_4, GPT_3_5_TURBO, etc.
  - RoleType: ASSISTANT, USER, SYSTEM
  - OpenAIBackendRole: ASSISTANT, SYSTEM, FUNCTION, TOOL
  - VectorDistance: DOT, COSINE, EUCLIDEAN

